<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- GP-2 (.superpowers/sdd/2026-07-28-wsg-plugin-connector-seam-blueprint/task-2-brief.md) — plain
         net10.0 (not -windows), matching St4i.Connector.Abstractions.csproj itself. This test project
         references ONLY that one assembly (see the ProjectReference below) — deliberately: a third-party
         driver author's own test suite for a sidecar built against the published contract would look
         exactly like this, with no St4i.EdgeCore/EngineApi/WPF host code in reach. If the round-trip test
         below only compiled because some host assembly's JSON options leaked in, that would prove
         nothing about the connector wire format actually being self-contained. -->
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Test-hygiene batch — the shared, disposable scratch root every test assembly installs before its
         first test runs (see tests/Shared/TestRunTempRoot.cs for the full rationale and the measured
         numbers). LINKED, not copied: one module initializer per assembly, one definition to maintain.
         Without it this suite writes into the real %TEMP% and the real %ProgramData%\ST4I\sim\creds and
         never cleans up either. -->
    <Compile Include="..\Shared\TestRunTempRoot.cs" Link="TestRunTempRoot.cs" />
    <!-- Task K-1 — the guard that measures the CONSEQUENCE rather than the naming: the REAL
         %ProgramData%\ST4I\sim\creds must not GAIN a file while this assembly's process runs (see
         tests/Shared/RealCredentialStoreLeakGuard.cs for what it does and does not see). LINKED into all
         five suites for the same reason as the line above — each process is its own measurement, and a
         guard installed in one suite says nothing about the other four.

         TWO THINGS ABOUT THIS PROJECT'S DELIBERATE ONE-REFERENCE BOUNDARY, and the second is a real cost
         rather than a footnote — the first draft of this comment asserted the first and introduced the
         second in the same clause (re-review Minor):
           * ASSEMBLY boundary: UNTOUCHED. The guard's only `using`s are System.* and Xunit; it adds no
             ProjectReference and cannot see St4i.EdgeCore. A third-party driver author's suite would
             still compile exactly as this one does.
           * TWO NEW DEPENDENCIES, and the first draft of this bullet named only one (branch review,
             Important 3 — "NEW DEPENDENCY" singular, in a project whose entire point is depending on as
             little as possible):
               (1) THE SOURCE TREE. It derives the directory by READING the product source, so this
                   project now requires being run from inside the tree. Off-tree execution yields
                   SetupFailure and a RED suite.
               (2) READ ACCESS TO A HARDENED MACHINE-WIDE DIRECTORY. The guard enumerates
                   %ProgramData%\ST4I\sim\creds, which SecurityDirAcl.Apply restricts to
                   SYSTEM/Administrators/owner on every CredentialStore.Save. A run under an identity
                   without read access there fails this suite — correctly, since it cannot measure — but
                   that is an environment requirement this project did not previously have.
             Both are fail-closed and deliberate: the alternative to (1) is a restated path literal that
             goes silently vacuous the day the store moves, and the alternative to (2) is treating "I
             could not look" as "nothing was there". Deliberate is not the same as free, which is why
             both are written down. -->
    <Compile Include="..\Shared\RealCredentialStoreLeakGuard.cs" Link="RealCredentialStoreLeakGuard.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.11.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.2" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="2.8.2" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\St4i.Connector.Abstractions\St4i.Connector.Abstractions.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
